# Optional on web/desktop; required for account access in native mobile apps.
# Leave empty for guest access on web/desktop. Native mobile stays at setup help.
# Obtain a publishable key from your Clerk application's API Keys page.
# Electron/iOS/Android: enable Native API and email-code sign-in/sign-up in Clerk.
# See .agents/reference/architecture/accounts.md for supported flows and token storage.
# Account management needs these Clerk dashboard settings: First and last name
# (to edit names) and "Allow users to delete their accounts" (to delete; App
# Store guideline 5.1.1(v) expects it once the app lets people create accounts).
# Connecting GitHub, Discord or Apple works on the web only.
# Never put a Clerk secret key in Vite client environment variables.
# Distribution builds use the GitHub repository variable of the same name;
# without it, Android/iPadOS builds offer only the temporary demo account.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# RevenueCat runs every subscription: Web Billing on web and desktop, the App
# Store and Google Play in the mobile apps. Set the public key for each, and
# the entitlement that unlocks Haptic Pro (default "pro"). Without a key, the
# Subscription page says subscriptions are not set up for the build.
VITE_REVENUECAT_WEB_API_KEY=
VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_API_KEY=
VITE_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_API_KEY=
VITE_REVENUECAT_PRO_ENTITLEMENT=

# Source Control device sign-in: the public client ids of a GitHub OAuth App
# with Device Flow enabled (repo and read:org scopes) and a non-confidential gitlab.com
# application with the device grant (api, write_repository scopes). Neither has
# a client secret. Without an id, that host's Sign In is hidden and a pasted
# token still works.
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GITLAB_CLIENT_ID=
